  "title": "2026-09-21-prompt-rag-162913 · rag-ingestion-retrieval",
  "description": "# RAG ingestion and retrieval\nRead the four bands top to bottom: ingestion, version-consistent publication, permission-aware query answering, and background model rebuilds.\n\nIngestion carries source ACLs through extraction, hash classification, overlapping chunks and rate-limited embeddings. Parse failures are quarantined without stopping the batch; transient embedding failures retry and exhausted batches retain inputs and attempt history for replay. Changed documents supersede old derived records; unchanged documents skip expensive work.\n\nPublication fans out to vector, document and keyword stores, then gates availability on matching versions in all three. Partial writes remain unavailable for repair or rollback. The wiki/42 example is illustrative, not an implementation schema.\n\nQueries fan out into vector and keyword searches, fuse and rerank, then filter by the asking user's permissions before generation. Only sufficient evidence permits a cited answer; thin context or uniformly low scores produces an abstention. Feedback and unanswered questions drive ingestion priorities.\n\nModel changes rebuild a new generation in the background. Live searches remain on the current generation until complete, consistent promotion; the prior generation is retained for rollback. This is a system-level design based on the supplied requirements, not a vendor-specific API diagram.",
  "mode": "diagram",
